            <ArticleTitle>Extent of myocardial ischemia during coronary occlusion in single vessel disease. A comparison between patients with exercise-induced angina and patients with recurrent angina at rest.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>433-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with exercise angina &gt;2 months (n:13) showed significantly lower SigmaST elevation during 120 s balloon coronary occlusion than those with =&lt;2 months (n:7), or those with angina at rest &lt;=2 days (n:8) but similar to patients with angina at rest &gt;2 days (n:7). These results underscore the importance of the kind and duration of angina in limiting the extent of ischemia during coronary occlusion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
